.TH PLOCK 8
.SH NAME
plock \- run a command while holding a lock on a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plock
[
.B \-r
]
[
.B \-t
]
.I lockfile
.I command
[
.I argument ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I plock
locks
.I lockfile
(creating it, mode 0600, if needed), runs the command with
.IR sh (1),
waits for it and releases the lock.  It is used in Diablo's adm scripts
to keep two runs of the same job from overlapping.  The arguments are
joined with spaces and passed to sh -c.  The exit status is the
command's.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Take a shared lock instead of an exclusive one.
.TP
.B \-t
Don't wait: if the lock is held, print "lock already held, exiting" and
exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
showlocks(8),
sh(1)
